1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,380
A Thank you.

2
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:37,060
At long last, we've finally found it.

3
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:39,060
No doubt.

4
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:40,720
Yes indeed.

5
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:49,240
Fifty long days of ferocious
battles on this journey

6
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:52,400
have all come down to this.

7
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:07,340
I don't see any signs of life.

8
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:10,720
Yeah, even the windows
are barred from inside.

9
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:13,060
It sure looks abandoned.

10
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:17,280
Jotaro, I'm sure you feel it too.

11
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,320
This deathly atmosphere.

12
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:24,020
A devil who possesses the
life force of darkness.

13
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:26,180
I'm certain it's Dio.

14
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:28,300
He's in there alright.

15
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,517
I'll take care of Dio.

16
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:37,320
The conclusion of this journey
ends a long chapter of my life.

17
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:41,880
No matter how powerful he is,
I'll cut him up with my own hands.

18
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:49,540
Polnareff, it is most dangerous
to go off on your own.

19
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:52,220
Once inside, you must follow Mr.

20
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,713
Joestar's instructions.

21
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:55,060
Is that understood?

22
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:59,464
There's no need for you
to worry so much, Avdol.

23
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:03,817
Don't tell me that after coming all this
way, you're starting to get cold feet.

24
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:04,730
What was that?

25
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,540
All right, then. Let's go.

26
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:17,255
You should look after that dumb dog
instead of worrying about what I do.

27
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:22,556
Although when the time comes,
he'll probably run away.

28
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:25,299
I will not force you to come along.

29
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:28,002
This will be our biggest battle.

30
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:30,359
We will risk our lives to fight it.

31
00:07:36,940 --> 00:07:39,705
I will leave you all of
the gum I have with me.

32
00:07:40,580 --> 00:07:45,197
If I should survive, I will personally
take you back to your hometown in New York.

33
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:46,400
I promise you.

34
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:05,757
I don't

35
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:12,800
know.

36
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:34,700
That settles that.

37
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:37,740
Looks like Dio already knows we're here.

38
00:08:40,420 --> 00:08:42,040
Let's bust him up.

39
00:08:55,680 --> 00:09:01,417
Hang on be strong holly
mrs joestar i i understand

40
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:04,317
how you feel but miss holly is in a coma.

41
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:08,217
Quite frankly she can't
hear you speak therefore

42
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:10,397
you really should go and rest for a while!

43
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:12,637
You haven't had any sleep for two days.

44
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,657
How dare you say something like that!

45
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:16,622
When her life hangs by a thread.

46
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:18,630
Lance's sake.

47
00:09:18,713 --> 00:09:21,277
Would joseph and jotaro
still half a world away?

48
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:22,889
At such a critical moment.

49
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:25,757
Who'd watch over her?

50
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:26,920
If i don't.

51
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:30,110
Jotaro.

52
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:31,730
Papa.

53
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:37,210
Jotaro.

54
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:39,200
I believe in you.

55
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:42,420
Holly, are you awake, dear?

56
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:44,460
Holly, Holly!

57
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:48,290
Mama,

58
00:09:48,373 --> 00:09:52,937
I know right now that Papa and Jotaro

59
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:56,917
are doing their best to save me.

60
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,580
I believe in them.

61
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:02,080
I can't believe it.

62
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:04,737
According to this, she
is still unconscious.

63
00:10:04,820 --> 00:10:05,650
Impossible.

64
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,529
How could she possibly
speak so coherently?

65
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:11,920
I believe in you, Jotaro.

66
00:10:12,620 --> 00:10:14,140
I believe.

67
00:10:15,660 --> 00:10:17,340
Be strong, Holly.

68
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:19,260
Believe in him.

69
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:22,240
Believe in your son, my grandson.

70
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:25,820
To believe in him is
our role in this battle.

71
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,546
There is something behind us!

72
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,100
Oh, damn it!

73
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:01,241
It's just a rat!

74
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:03,171
Don't scare me like that!

75
00:11:30,260 --> 00:11:31,400
This is it.

76
00:11:31,740 --> 00:11:33,340
It is Dio's coffin.

77
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:44,541
I'm going to let the sunlight in.

78
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:58,860
We've known this man we're about to meet
since before Jotaro and I were even born.

79
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:04,200
Yes, the blood of the Joestars
knows this man all too well.

80
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:08,417
The battle we are about to begin.

81
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:12,577
No matter what the
outcome, I have no regrets.

82
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:13,877
I am here.

83
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,877
Because I want no regrets.

84
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:20,677
Well, how long are we
going to stare at it?

85
00:12:20,760 --> 00:12:23,317
If no one else is going to
do it, then I'll open it.

86
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:24,657
Do not be so careless.

87
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:29,977
What careless did I hear
you say? You think I'm?

88
00:12:30,060 --> 00:12:33,900
careless mr.

89
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:36,917
Joestar allow me to use my fire here

90
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:43,180
hey you better not ignore me Stay back!

91
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:38,060
This is... What the?

92
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,480
Why am I here?

93
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:54,800
Oh, how did that happen?

94
00:13:57,140 --> 00:13:57,970
Abdo!

95
00:13:58,920 --> 00:13:59,861
Wait, stay back!

96
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:02,120
Old man?

97
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:04,180
Jotaro, you too.

98
00:14:04,660 --> 00:14:05,660
Think about this.

99
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:07,897
Think about what has just happened.

100
00:14:07,980 --> 00:14:10,320
If we're not careful, we'll all die.

101
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,110
Dio?

102
00:14:12,193 --> 00:14:13,023
Was it Dio?

103
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:14,820
That bastard, where is he?

104
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:16,720
What did he do to you?

105
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:19,060
Get away, Polnareff.

106
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:21,660
You've got to run now.

107
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:23,030
Run.

108
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:36,817
You have finally arrived.

109
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:41,480
I must congratulate you
all for your efforts.

110
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,740
You bastard!

111
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:47,120
So then you're... Dio.

112
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:51,800
I know Dio's secret.

113
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:53,040
His stand.

114
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:57,157
His secret is he's able to...

115
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:58,560
Do it.

116
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:00,100
Get away!

117
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:24,800
Come over here by me.

118
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:31,340
His name is Iced.

119
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:33,933
You may have heard about him from Darby.

120
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:39,600
I took him under my wing, and
he has become my right-hand man.

121
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:42,377
What did you do to Avdol?

122
00:15:42,460 --> 00:15:43,813
What did you do to him?

123
00:15:44,180 --> 00:15:45,440
Where is he, Dio?

124
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:48,020
You need to calm down, Polnareff.

125
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:50,420
Why are you so anxious all the time?

126
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:54,380
Are you afraid of me, Dio?

127
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:57,480
Look at him.

128
00:15:57,720 --> 00:16:00,040
He obeys me without question.

129
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:02,900
Without any fear or anxiety whatsoever.

130
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:07,200
Hey, Iced. I know.

131
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:10,000
Why don't you cut your head off?

132
00:16:18,960 --> 00:16:23,200
Can you understand why
he obeys me so blindly?

133
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:27,520
It is because he feels
secure about serving me.

134
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:34,100
Many have been alienated by society
because of the superior power they possess,

135
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:35,820
their stand abilities.

136
00:16:36,140 --> 00:16:37,540
But by serving me,

137
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:42,200
worthless feelings like loneliness
and insecurity are gone for good.

138
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:43,780
Do you know why?

139
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:50,100
It is because I, Dio, am the
ultimate, absolute power.

140
00:16:56,360 --> 00:17:02,120
A worthy man such as Eist shouldn't
be left to die in a place like this.

141
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:10,120
May you resurrect with the
blood from my veins, Eist.

142
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:17,310
Well,

143
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:19,297
now back to the four of you,

144
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:24,840
who came all the way to Egypt with some
crazed notion of killing me, no doubt.

145
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:28,300
Uh, Joseph and Jotaro?

146
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:33,300
I must give you the
punishment of absolute death.

147
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:37,040
I must end my karma
with the Jostar family.

148
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:44,120
However, Polnareff, it would be
such a waste to have to kill you.

149
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:48,100
You are an unbelievably
talented stand-user.

150
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:51,060
What do you say?

151
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:53,222
Why don't you become my servant?

152
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:55,900
You, along with that dog over there.

153
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:58,760
And if you do decide to become my servant,

154
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:03,400
both of you will have the absolute
security of never fearing death again.

155
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:06,480
Shut your mouth. What?

156
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:09,780
You must be hard of hearing!

157
00:18:10,180 --> 00:18:13,300
Shut your mouth, Dio,
and answer my question!

158
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:15,148
What did you do with Avdol?

159
00:18:15,340 --> 00:18:17,700
I'm asking you, where did you take him?

160
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:22,357
Why bother yourself
with such petty details?

161
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:24,720
Why don't you tell him, Iced?

162
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:29,160
Your friend Avdol is dead.

163
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:34,537
He was swallowed up by a sub-dimension my

164
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:37,720
stand created and has
disappeared without a trace.

165
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:42,820
Where Avdol has gone is
a mystery, even to me.

166
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:47,220
You bastard!

167
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:51,620
Ah, what pressure.

168
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:57,720
It is such a waste to
kill a man like yourself.

169
00:18:58,100 --> 00:18:59,860
But then, so be it.

170
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:01,880
Deal with him, iced.

171
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:09,300
Shut your mouth!

172
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:19,010
Cheap!

173
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:21,870
What?

174
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:29,460
Hold the wrap!

175
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:37,840
Boy, old man, you should feel honored.

176
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:41,007
I, Dio, am going to deal
with you personally.

177
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:54,780
Did the dog run away?

178
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:59,557
It would certainly
appear that that dog has

179
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:02,052
more brains than the two of you combined.

180
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:05,420
You bastard.

181
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:16,540
Damn it.

182
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:19,980
What now?

183
00:20:20,340 --> 00:20:21,500
Where did he go to?

184
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:39,420
This is crazy!

185
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:03,200
Bastard.

186
00:21:03,660 --> 00:21:06,720
He absorbs everything
in his path as he moves.

187
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:10,300
This is not good.

188
00:21:10,840 --> 00:21:13,016
There's nowhere around to take cover.

189
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:15,480
I'd better move.

190
00:21:25,840 --> 00:21:28,500
Notice I took a chunk
out of your foot first,

191
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:31,468
so you won't be able
to scurry off anywhere.

192
00:21:31,740 --> 00:21:34,217
I will have to discipline
you for foolishly

193
00:21:34,300 --> 00:21:37,300
thinking you can disobey
the all-powerful Lord Dio.

194
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:38,717
Where do you want it next?

195
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:40,640
Your arm or in your gut?

196
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:42,630
Bastard!

197
00:21:48,260 --> 00:21:50,080
A spray.

198
00:22:12,480 --> 00:22:15,540
My sword can only cut him
when he's not invisible.

199
00:22:16,780 --> 00:22:19,200
Dio, why you... No, wait!

200
00:22:28,500 --> 00:22:29,700
What the...

201
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,500
What's wrong?

202
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:35,821
How long are you planning
to take to come up here?

203
00:22:37,600 --> 00:22:38,430
You...

204
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:43,460
Just what are you attacking?

205
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:45,310
What?

206
00:22:45,393 --> 00:22:46,223
When did you?

207
00:22:48,580 --> 00:22:50,440
He never even moved.

208
00:22:50,900 --> 00:22:52,240
Is this his stand?

209
00:22:53,520 --> 00:22:58,500
Well, to tell you the truth, Joseph, there
is a little something I need from you.

210
00:22:58,900 --> 00:23:03,100
To be perfectly precise, Joseph,
I need fresh blood from you.

211
00:23:04,060 --> 00:23:04,890
What's that?

212
00:23:04,973 --> 00:23:10,340
From the neck down, this body is that of
my long-standing enemy, Jonathan Joestar,

213
00:23:10,660 --> 00:23:13,260
and it is not a comfortable fit just yet.

214
00:23:14,700 --> 00:23:21,320
Among all the humans alive, Joseph, you
are the Joestar family's oldest survivor.

215
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:25,260
Do you get it?

216
00:23:25,540 --> 00:23:29,560
Your blood matches Jonathan's
more closely than anyone else's.

217
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:31,790
Jotaro!

218
00:23:31,873 --> 00:23:32,703
Get out!

219
00:23:32,940 --> 00:23:33,770
What?

220
00:23:36,940 --> 00:23:39,220
By sucking your fresh blood,

221
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:41,460
I will fully conquer this body,

222
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:44,937
and I shall put an end to this
karma with the Joestar family

223
00:23:45,020 --> 00:23:48,740
that has plagued me for one
hundred long and tiresome years.

224
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:52,900
It's only me he's after.
Hurry up! Get away!

225
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:54,277
Don't give me that!

226
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:56,125
Why the hell should I run now?

227
00:23:56,760 --> 00:24:01,220
It would be wise to listen to
your elders in this case, Jotaro.

228
00:24:03,360 --> 00:24:07,140
Although, I have no intention
of letting you go that easily.

229
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:33,480
This isn't about speed or playing tricks.

230
00:24:34,080 --> 00:24:36,320
Could this be Dio's stand? And?

231
00:24:36,440 --> 00:24:38,460
The power of the world?

232
00:24:40,500 --> 00:24:42,280
Well, you old fool.

233
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:46,540
You mark the end.

234
00:25:09,820 --> 00:25:12,040
You're so persistent.

235
00:25:40,360 --> 00:25:42,460
Oh, my God. Damn it.

236
00:25:42,900 --> 00:25:44,240
My entire body.

237
00:25:44,600 --> 00:25:46,360
I can't move.

238
00:25:46,780 --> 00:25:51,604
It's not for very long, but you really
should thank Avdol for extending your life.

239
00:25:53,260 --> 00:25:56,436
In that fleeting moment, if
he hadn't pushed you away,

240
00:25:56,640 --> 00:25:59,934
you would have been swallowed
up into the sub-dimension.

241
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:04,760
He could have survived if he tried to
escape by himself and not save you.

242
00:26:07,620 --> 00:26:09,500
What a complete idiot.

243
00:26:10,460 --> 00:26:12,480
Did you say idiot?

244
00:26:13,540 --> 00:26:16,860
It said the more foolish you
are, the younger you die.

245
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:19,420
Damn you!

246
00:26:25,860 --> 00:26:26,690
Ha!

247
00:26:26,773 --> 00:26:28,540
I see you can still move.

248
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:30,880
But this is the end of a line.

249
00:26:31,180 --> 00:26:35,592
After I send you to hell, you'll have
a long time to regret your stupidity.

250
00:26:42,740 --> 00:26:43,570
Hm?

251
00:26:49,500 --> 00:26:50,330
Whoa!

252
00:26:55,700 --> 00:26:56,530
Oh! Oh!

253
00:26:56,613 --> 00:26:57,443
Oh!

254
00:27:05,500 --> 00:27:06,340
Iggy!

255
00:27:07,020 --> 00:27:08,420
You...

256
00:27:11,480 --> 00:27:12,597
You came...

257
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:14,400
to my rescue.

258
00:27:17,280 --> 00:27:18,257
So sorry.

259
00:27:18,340 --> 00:27:21,660
I thought you'd be long gone by now.

260
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:25,965
I didn't even think of
you as part of our team.

261
00:27:27,180 --> 00:27:29,240
But then you saved me.

262
00:27:33,300 --> 00:27:34,740
Thanks a lot, Iggy.

263
00:27:35,460 --> 00:27:37,560
You were able to avenge Avdol.

264
00:27:38,260 --> 00:27:40,789
I wish I could have
done it myself, though.

265
00:27:43,840 --> 00:27:45,600
Iggy, get out of here!

266
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:47,300
He's still alive!

267
00:27:49,580 --> 00:27:50,410
